---
// The playground: a reader on a text of your own, with what it starts from (view, pace, language, where it sits)
// and its theme set from the page, and the code that gives the same reader. Everything stays in the browser.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const samples = [
  {
    id: 'en',
    label: 'English',
    lang: 'en',
    text: `# Reading, a few words at a time

Most of what we read on a screen asks the eye to do two jobs at once: follow the words, and find its way back to the line after every glance away. The focus reader takes the second job off its hands.

It shows the text a few words at a time, in the same place, at a pace you choose. A comma makes a frame stay a beat longer, the end of a sentence two, and the whole is scaled so the rate shown is the rate you get.

Reading back matters more than reading fast. Pause, and the sentence shows under the band; the arrows, a scroll or a swipe go a frame back or on.`,
  },
  {
    id: 'fr',
    label: 'Français',
    lang: 'fr',
    text: `# Lire autrement

Un texte peut se lire de plusieurs façons. Sur le papier, l'œil suit une ligne, saute à la suivante, revient en arrière quand il a perdu le fil, et personne ne le remarque.

Ici, le texte avance seul, au rythme choisi. Les mots déjà lus s'estompent, ceux qui restent attendent, et la ligne en cours reste toujours au même endroit.

Une virgule retient le regard un instant, la fin d'une phrase un peu plus, et le débit affiché reste celui que vous obtenez.`,
  },
  {
    id: 'ja',
    label: '日本語',
    lang: 'ja',
    text: `# 吾輩は猫である

吾輩は猫である。名前はまだ無い。

どこで生れたかとんと見当がつかぬ。何でも薄暗いじめじめした所でニャーニャー泣いていた事だけは記憶している。吾輩はここで始めて人間というものを見た。`,
  },
];
const langs = [
  ['en', 'English'],
  ['fr', 'French'],
  ['de', 'German'],
  ['es', 'Spanish'],
  ['it', 'Italian'],
  ['pt', 'Portuguese'],
  ['ja', 'Japanese'],
  ['zh', 'Chinese'],
  ['th', 'Thai'],
];
const colors = [
  ['paper', 'Paper'],
  ['ink', 'Ink'],
  ['muted', 'Muted'],
  ['accent', 'Accent'],
];
const fonts = [
  ['', 'The site’s (Figtree)'],
  ['system-ui, sans-serif', 'System sans'],
  ['Georgia, serif', 'Serif (Georgia)'],
  ['ui-monospace, monospace', 'Monospace'],
];
---

<Base title="Playground" description="Read your own text in the focus reader, set how it starts and how it looks, and copy the code.">
  <div class="column head">
    <p class="type-label kind">Playground</p>
    <h1>Read your own text</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Paste a text, set how the reader starts and how it looks, and copy the code that gives the same one. Nothing leaves this page: the text stays in your
      browser.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="column bench" id="playground" data-samples={JSON.stringify(samples)}>
    <div class="stage">
      <div class="tile" id="tile">
        <p class="waiting">The playground needs JavaScript.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        The controls set where the reader <em>starts</em>; its own panel takes over from there. Space plays and pauses, the arrows go a frame back or on.
      </p>
    </div>

    <form class="controls" id="controls" autocomplete="off">
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="type-label">Text</legend>
        <div class="segmented" id="samples">
          {
            samples.map((s) => (
              <button type="button" class="btn" data-sample={s.id} lang={s.lang}>
                {s.label}
              </button>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="text">The text to read</label>
        <textarea id="text" rows="9" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Paste a text here. A blank line separates paragraphs; a line starting with # is a heading."></textarea>
        <div class="row">
          <label for="lang">Language</label>
          <select id="lang" name="lang">
            {langs.map(([v, l]) => <option value={v}>{l}</option>)}
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <label for="heading">Heading</label>
          <input id="heading" name="heading" type="text" value="My text" />
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend class="type-label">Where it starts</legend>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="lbl" id="l-view">View</span>
          <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-labelledby="l-view" data-choice="view">
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="sequence">Sequence</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="flow">Flow</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <label for="wpm">Speed</label>
          <input id="wpm" name="wpm" type="range" min="100" max="800" step="25" />
          <output for="wpm" id="wpm-out"></output>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <label for="words">Words</label>
          <input id="words" name="words" type="range" min="1" max="6" step="1" />
          <output for="words" id="words-out"></output>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="lbl" id="l-size">Size</span>
          <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-labelledby="l-size" data-choice="size">
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="s">S</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="m">M</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="l">L</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="xl">XL</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row" data-only="sequence">
          <span class="lbl" id="l-align">Align</span>
          <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-labelledby="l-align" data-choice="align">
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="left">Left</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="center">Centre</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="pivot">Pivot</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row" data-only="flow">
          <span class="lbl" id="l-underline">Underline</span>
          <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-labelledby="l-underline" data-choice="underline">
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="on">On</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="off">Off</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="lbl" id="l-place">Placement</span>
          <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-labelledby="l-place" data-choice="place">
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="inline">In the page</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-value="modal">Over the page</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend class="type-label">Theme · <span id="scheme">light</span></legend>
        <p class="hint">Colours are kept for the theme the page is in: switch it in the header to set the other.</p>
        <div class="swatches">
          {
            colors.map(([key, label]) => (
              <label class="swatch">
                <input type="color" data-color={key} />
                <span>{label}</span>
              </label>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <label for="font">Typeface</label>
          <select id="font" name="font">
            {fonts.map(([v, l]) => <option value={v}>{l}</option>)}
          </select>
        </div>
        <p><button type="button" class="btn" id="reset">Back to the site’s theme</button></p>
      </fieldset>
    </form>
  </div>

  <div class="column out">
    <div class="out-head">
      <div class="segmented" role="tablist" aria-label="The code as">
        <button type="button" class="btn" role="tab" data-code="html" aria-selected="true">HTML</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn" role="tab" data-code="astro" aria-selected="false">Astro</button>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-copy-from="code">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre class="code"><code id="code"></code></pre>
    <p class="note">
      Only what differs from the defaults is written. See <a href={url('docs/attributes/')}>Attributes</a> and <a href={url('docs/theming/')}>Theming</a> for
      the rest.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  import type { FocusReader } from '../../../src/element.ts';

  type View = 'sequence' | 'flow';
  type Scheme = 'light' | 'dark';
  type ColorKey = 'paper' | 'ink' | 'muted' | 'accent';
  interface Sample {
    id: string;
    lang: string;
    text: string;
  }

  const root = document.documentElement;
  const bench = document.getElementById('playground')!;
  const tile = document.getElementById('tile')!;
  const form = document.getElementById('controls') as HTMLFormElement;
  const textarea = document.getElementById('text') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
  const code = document.getElementById('code')!;
  const samples: Sample[] = JSON.parse(bench.dataset.samples!);
  const $ = <T extends HTMLElement>(id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as T;

  // the element's own defaults: what is not written in the code
  const PACE = { sequence: { wpm: 150, words: 1, size: 'm' }, flow: { wpm: 300, words: 6, size: 'm' } };
  const PROPS: Record<ColorKey, string> = { paper: '--fr-paper', ink: '--fr-ink', muted: '--fr-muted', accent: '--fr-accent' };
  // the site's own colour behind each, to show in the pickers before any is changed
  const TOKENS: Record<ColorKey, string> = { paper: '--color-paper', ink: '--color-ink', muted: '--color-text-muted', accent: '--color-citron' };

  const state = {
    text: samples[0].text,
    sample: samples[0].id as string | null,
    lang: samples[0].lang,
    heading: 'My text',
    view: 'sequence' as View,
    pace: structuredClone(PACE) as Record<View, { wpm: number; words: number; size: string }>,
    align: 'left',
    underline: 'on',
    place: 'inline',
    theme: { light: {}, dark: {} } as Record<Scheme, Partial<Record<ColorKey, string>>>,
    font: '',
    code: 'html' as 'html' | 'astro',
  };
  let reader: FocusReader | null = null;

  const scheme = (): Scheme =>
    root.dataset.theme === 'light' || root.dataset.theme === 'dark' ? root.dataset.theme : matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';

  // ——— the reader

  /** The attributes that differ from the element's defaults, in the order the docs give them. */
  function attributes(): [string, string][] {
    const pace = state.pace[state.view];
    const base = PACE[state.view];
    const out: [string, string][] = [];
    if (state.heading) out.push(['heading', state.heading]);
    if (state.lang !== 'en') out.push(['lang', state.lang]);
    if (state.view !== 'sequence') out.push(['view', state.view]);
    if (pace.wpm !== base.wpm) out.push(['wpm', String(pace.wpm)]);
    if (pace.words !== base.words) out.push(['words', String(pace.words)]);
    if (pace.size !== base.size) out.push(['size', pace.size]);
    if (state.view === 'sequence' && state.align !== 'left') out.push(['align', state.align]);
    if (state.view === 'flow' && state.underline === 'off') out.push(['underline', 'off']);
    if (state.place === 'modal') out.push(['modal', '']);
    return out;
  }

  /** The theme's declarations for a scheme: the accent does for its text too. */
  function declarations(s: Scheme, withFont: boolean): [string, string][] {
    const out: [string, string][] = [];
    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(state.theme[s]) as [ColorKey, string][]) {
      out.push([PROPS[key], value]);
      if (key === 'accent') out.push(['--fr-accent-text', value]);
    }
    if (withFont && state.font) out.push(['--fr-font-text', state.font]);
    return out;
  }

  function paint() {
    if (!reader) return;
    for (const prop of [...Object.values(PROPS), '--fr-accent-text', '--fr-font-text']) reader.style.removeProperty(prop);
    for (const [prop, value] of declarations(scheme(), true)) reader.style.setProperty(prop, value);
  }

  /** A new reader for the settings: they are read once, when it joins the page. */
  function build() {
    const next = document.createElement('focus-reader') as FocusReader;
    for (const [name, value] of attributes()) next.setAttribute(name, value);
    next.textContent = state.text;
    next.addEventListener('focusreaderview', (e) => {
      state.view = (e as CustomEvent<{ view: View }>).detail.view;
      controls();
      write();
    });
    reader = next;
    paint();
    tile.replaceChildren(next);
    if (state.place === 'modal') {
      const open = document.createElement('button');
      open.type = 'button';
      open.className = 'btn primary open';
      open.textContent = 'Open the reader';
      open.addEventListener('click', () => next.open());
      tile.append(open);
    }
    write();
  }

  // ——— the code

  const esc = (s: string) => s.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
  const css = (decl: [string, string][], pad: string) => decl.map(([p, v]) => `${pad}${p}: ${v};`).join('\n');

  function html() {
    const attrs = [['for', 'article-body'], ...attributes()].map(([n, v]) => (v ? `${n}="${esc(v)}"` : n));
    const tag = attrs.join(' ').length > 70 ? `<focus-reader\n  ${attrs.join('\n  ')}\n></focus-reader>` : `<focus-reader ${attrs.join(' ')}></focus-reader>`;
    const lines: string[] = [];
    if (state.place === 'modal') lines.push(`<button onclick="document.querySelector('focus-reader').open()">Focus</button>`);
    lines.push(tag, `<script type="module" src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/focus-reader/dist/src/register.js"><\/script>`);
    const light = declarations('light', true);
    const dark = declarations('dark', false);
    if (light.length || dark.length) {
      lines.push('', '<style>');
      if (light.length) lines.push(`  focus-reader {\n${css(light, '    ')}\n  }`);
      if (dark.length) lines.push(`  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n    focus-reader {\n${css(dark, '      ')}\n    }\n  }`);
      lines.push('</style>');
    }
    return lines.join('\n');
  }

  const js = (v: unknown) => (typeof v === 'string' ? `'${v.replace(/'/g, "\\'")}'` : String(v));
  const obj = (entries: [string, unknown][]) => `{ ${entries.map(([k, v]) => `${k}: ${js(v)}`).join(', ')} }`;

  function astro() {
    const options: string[] = [];
    if (state.view !== 'sequence') options.push(`view: 'flow',`);
    for (const view of ['sequence', 'flow'] as View[]) {
      const pace = state.pace[view];
      const base = PACE[view];
      const entries: [string, unknown][] = [];
      if (pace.wpm !== base.wpm) entries.push(['wpm', pace.wpm]);
      if (pace.words !== base.words) entries.push(['words', pace.words]);
      if (pace.size !== base.size) entries.push(['size', pace.size]);
      if (view === 'sequence' && state.align !== 'left') entries.push(['align', state.align]);
      if (view === 'flow' && state.underline === 'off') entries.push(['underline', false]);
      if (entries.length) options.push(`${view}: ${obj(entries)},`);
    }
    const theme: string[] = [];
    for (const s of ['light', 'dark'] as Scheme[]) {
      const entries = Object.entries(state.theme[s]).flatMap(([k, v]): [string, unknown][] => (k === 'accent' ? [[k, v], ['accentText', v]] : [[k, v]]));
      if (entries.length) theme.push(`${s}: ${obj(entries)},`);
    }
    if (state.font) theme.push(`fonts: { text: ${js(state.font)} },`);
    if (theme.length) options.push(`theme: {\n      ${theme.join('\n      ')}\n    },`);
    const call = options.length ? `focusReader({\n    ${options.join('\n    ')}\n  })` : 'focusReader()';
    const props = [state.heading && `heading="${esc(state.heading)}"`, state.lang !== 'en' && `lang="${state.lang}"`, state.place === 'inline' && 'inline'].filter(Boolean);
    const open = `<FocusReader${props.length ? ' ' + props.join(' ') : ''}`;
    const use = state.place === 'inline' ? `${open} for="article-body" />` : `${open}>\n  <article><Content /></article>\n</FocusReader>`;
    return `// astro.config.mjs
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';
import focusReader from 'focus-reader/astro';

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [${call}],
});

---
// a page
import FocusReader from 'focus-reader/astro/FocusReader.astro';
---
${use}`;
  }

  function write() {
    code.textContent = state.code === 'html' ? html() : astro();
  }

  // ——— the controls

  /** The controls as the state has them. */
  function controls() {
    const pace = state.pace[state.view];
    const choices: Record<string, string> = { view: state.view, size: pace.size, align: state.align, underline: state.underline, place: state.place };
    for (const group of form.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-choice]')) {
      for (const b of group.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button')) b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b.dataset.value === choices[group.dataset.choice!]));
    }
    for (const b of form.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-sample]')) b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b.dataset.sample === state.sample));
    for (const row of form.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-only]')) row.hidden = row.dataset.only !== state.view;
    $<HTMLInputElement>('wpm').value = String(pace.wpm);
    $('wpm-out').textContent = `${pace.wpm} wpm`;
    $<HTMLInputElement>('words').value = String(pace.words);
    $('words-out').textContent = String(pace.words);
    $<HTMLSelectElement>('lang').value = state.lang;
    $<HTMLSelectElement>('font').value = state.font;
    if (textarea.value !== state.text) textarea.value = state.text;
    swatches();
  }

  /** The pickers show the colours of the theme the page is in: the ones chosen, else the site's own. */
  function swatches() {
    const s = scheme();
    $('scheme').textContent = s;
    const style = getComputedStyle(root);
    for (const input of form.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-color]')) {
      const key = input.dataset.color as ColorKey;
      input.value = (state.theme[s][key] ?? style.getPropertyValue(TOKENS[key]).trim()).toLowerCase();
    }
  }

  for (const group of form.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-choice]')) {
    group.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-value]');
      if (!b) return;
      const key = group.dataset.choice!;
      const value = b.dataset.value!;
      if (key === 'view') state.view = value as View;
      else if (key === 'size') state.pace[state.view].size = value;
      else if (key === 'align') state.align = value;
      else if (key === 'underline') state.underline = value;
      else state.place = value;
      controls();
      build();
    });
  }
  for (const id of ['wpm', 'words'] as const) {
    const input = $<HTMLInputElement>(id);
    // the figure follows the slider; the reader is rebuilt once it is let go
    input.addEventListener('input', () => {
      state.pace[state.view][id] = Number(input.value);
      controls();
      write();
    });
    input.addEventListener('change', build);
  }
  $('samples').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-sample]');
    const sample = samples.find((s) => s.id === b?.dataset.sample);
    if (!sample) return;
    Object.assign(state, { text: sample.text, sample: sample.id, lang: sample.lang });
    controls();
    build();
  });
  let typing = 0;
  textarea.addEventListener('input', () => {
    state.text = textarea.value;
    state.sample = null;
    controls();
    clearTimeout(typing);
    // the same reader reads the new text, keeping its place
    typing = window.setTimeout(() => {
      if (!reader) return;
      reader.textContent = state.text;
      reader.reload();
    }, 300);
  });
  $<HTMLSelectElement>('lang').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.lang = (e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value;
    build();
  });
  $<HTMLInputElement>('heading').addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    state.heading = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).value;
    reader?.setAttribute('heading', state.heading);
    write();
  });
  for (const input of form.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-color]')) {
    input.addEventListener('input', () => {
      state.theme[scheme()][input.dataset.color as ColorKey] = input.value;
      paint();
      write();
    });
  }
  $<HTMLSelectElement>('font').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.font = (e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value;
    paint();
    write();
  });
  $('reset').addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.theme = { light: {}, dark: {} };
    state.font = '';
    controls();
    paint();
    write();
  });
  form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => e.preventDefault());

  for (const tab of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-code]')) {
    tab.addEventListener('click', () => {
      state.code = tab.dataset.code as 'html' | 'astro';
      for (const t of document.querySelectorAll('[data-code]')) t.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(t === tab));
      write();
    });
  }

  // the page changed theme, from its switch or from the system's: the reader and the pickers follow
  const retheme = () => {
    swatches();
    paint();
  };
  new MutationObserver(retheme).observe(root, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['data-theme'] });
  matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').addEventListener('change', retheme);

  controls();
  customElements.whenDefined('focus-reader').then(build);
</script>

<style>
  .head {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
  }
  .kind {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
    font-family: var(--type-display-family);
    font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    line-height: var(--type-display-line-height);
  }
  .standfirst {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bench {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 22rem;
    gap: var(--spacing-xl);
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
  }
  .stage {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-h) + var(--spacing-lg));
  }
  .tile {
    height: min(600px, calc(100dvh - var(--header-h) - 120px));
    min-height: 420px;
    background: var(--color-paper-deep);
  }
  .tile :global(.open) {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 50% auto auto 50%;
    translate: -50% -50%;
  }
  .waiting {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .note,
  .hint {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
    font-size: var(--type-caption-size);
    line-height: var(--type-caption-line-height);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  fieldset {
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 0 var(--spacing-lg);
    border: 0;
  }
  fieldset + fieldset {
    padding-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-top: var(--spacing-hairline) solid var(--color-ink);
  }
  /* floated, the legend sits inside the fieldset, under its hairline, instead of on it */
  legend {
    float: left;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  legend + * {
    clear: both;
  }
  #samples {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  textarea {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border: var(--spacing-hairline) solid var(--color-ink);
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text-strong);
